---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — learninghub"
  description="Why learninghub exists and how these deep-dives are written."
>
  <section class="about wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Learning in public, one system at a time.</h1>

    <div class="body">
      <p>
        Every article here starts as a personal study log: a syllabus, a set of
        pass/fail checks, and a running list of the things I got <em>wrong</em>
        and had to relearn. When a topic clicks, I rewrite those notes as a
        deep-dive meant for someone standing where I was a few weeks ago.
      </p>

      <h2>How each deep-dive is built</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Mental model first.</strong> Before any API, the one idea that makes the rest make sense.</li>
        <li><strong>Taught to a rubric.</strong> Each section maps to a concrete "can you actually do this?" check, not just exposure.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Gotchas are first-class.</strong> The
          <span class="tag" style="--accent:#c2410c">⚠ Gotcha</span>
          boxes are real mistakes from my review queue — the misconceptions that
          cost me a session to unlearn, so they cost you a minute.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Verified, not remembered.</strong> Version-specific facts are checked against current docs before publishing.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        The goal isn't a reference you skim — it's understanding you keep. If a
        section can't survive being explained back in your own words, it isn't
        done.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .about { max-width: 44rem; padding-top: 3rem; }
    .about h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3rem); margin: 0.6rem 0 2rem; }
    .body { font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7; }
    .body h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 0.6rem; }
    .body ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
    .body li { margin: 0.7rem 0; }
    .body li::marker { color: var(--accent); }
    .body em { color: var(--accent-ink); font-style: italic; }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
